# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies (anywhere — the kitchen/ and tablet/ panels install their own)
node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# IDE/AI tools - NEVER commit these... with two deliberate exceptions.
#
# Everything under .claude/ stays out (settings.local.json holds this machine's command
# approvals, .vercel2.token is a secret, worktrees/ is 17 GB, sweep/ is scratch).
#
# BUT the "cannot be forgotten" guards are wired to an edit ONLY by .claude/settings.json, and
# that file being ignored meant the enforcement existed on exactly one laptop: no clone, no CI,
# and none of the 28 git worktrees had it. Nothing printed a warning; an unguarded session
# looked identical to a guarded one. So the hook config and the hook it runs are versioned.
# It was FOUR when this was written (verify:ui, verify:taps, verify:test-safety, verify:audit);
# it is NINE now — read the PostToolUse command in .claude/settings.json for the live list
# rather than trusting a count here, which is exactly how this comment went stale.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/*
!.claude/hooks/health-nudge.mjs

# Private local menu editor (uses the service-role key — never push it).
# Anchored with a leading slash so it ONLY ignores the ROOT editor/ — NOT the
# new app/editor/ route that's part of the unified app.
/editor/

# vercel
.vercel

# local launcher scripts (machine-specific — never commit)
*.bat
# The exception below is KEPT but is currently DEAD, and that is the honest state: there is no
# public/print-station/ folder and nothing ships a .bat any more. We tried it and it failed —
# macOS Gatekeeper and Windows SmartScreen flag a script because it ARRIVED FROM THE WEB, so the
# owner met "could not verify it is free of malware" with only Done or Move to Bin. Since
# 2026-08-19 /print-setup.html TEACHES the reader to type the file themselves, one menu per OS
# (docs/KITCHEN-PRINT-SETUP.md §9; guarded by `npm run verify:print-helper`, which fails if
# anything is offered as a download again). Do not re-add a ⬇ button on the strength of this line.
!public/print-station/*.bat

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# health-nudge hook state (per-machine prompt counter — not code)
.claude/hooks/health-nudge-state.json
verify-*.png

# pre-rewrite reference: the bulky frozen code copy is preserved by the
# `pre-rewrite-reference` git tag, so don't also commit a full duplicate.
# The small docs (README.md, DATABASE.md) ARE committed for convenience.
reference/code-snapshot/

# brainstorm companion mockups (local only)
.superpowers/

# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/

# Throwaway admin dashboard prototypes (local scratch). They render real per-restaurant
# food revenue and their local server pulls the earnings API with an admin cookie — the
# admin panel must show NO money, so these must NEVER be committed or wired into the app.
temp-admin-analytics/
temp-admin-console/

# ── gaps found by the tooling sweeps (2026-08-04, 2026-08-05) ─────────────────
# `/.next/` above is ANCHORED and exact, so a dev server on another port creates a
# fully committable build directory (.next-8093/ was sitting here untracked).
.next-*/
# Throwaway probe scripts. verify:ui catches these AFTER they are committed;
# ignoring them stops it happening at all. Two such files at the repo root were
# signing in to the live client site when the 2026-08-04 sweep found them.
/_*.mjs
/_*.js
/_*.ts
# Handoff notes are temp files by definition — the session that picks one up deletes it.
/*-HANDOFF.md
# Local research/scratch output
docs/research/
# Other AI tools' per-machine state. These were TRACKED, and .agents/ was also the
# only CRLF content in the repo (67 files of image-generation marketing skills, which
# have nothing to do with a restaurant billing app).
.agents/
.codex/

# ── Big things that live on this Mac, not in the repo (T10 sweep, 2026-08-12) ────────────────
# 186 tracked files / 26 MB that no build, no deploy and no test has ever read. .vercelignore
# already kept them out of deploys (that was the expensive half); this keeps them out of every
# clone and every worktree, which matters in a repo that runs 20 parallel sessions.
#
# THE FILES ARE STILL ON DISK — `git rm --cached` only stopped tracking them. Nothing was deleted.
# Competitor research: 185 screenshots + a macOS .app bundle (with spaces in its path).
/All_compitior_POs_INFO/
# The owner's handover PDF (760 KB, last changed 2026-07-25). Read by a person, never by the app.
/PROJECT-HANDOFF.pdf
